cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "react-native-dl-scan: On-Device Driver's License Scanning for React Native"
message: >-
  If you use this software or the bundled ML models in academic work,
  please cite both this repository and the IDNet dataset used for training
  (see preferred-citation below and docs/DATA_CARD.md).
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hicks
    given-names: Shannon
    orcid: ""
    email: shan@iotashan.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/iotashan/react-native-dl-scan"
url: "https://github.com/iotashan/react-native-dl-scan"
license: MIT
version: "0.2.0"
date-released: "2026-05-28"
abstract: >-
  A React Native library for real-time on-device scanning of US and Canadian
  driver's licenses and ICAO 9303 MRZ documents. Bundles two Apache-2.0 ML models (a DocAligner document-rectification model
  and a NanoDet-Plus-m field detector) trained/fine-tuned on the IDNet synthetic
  identity document dataset, run on-device via react-native-fast-tflite (Core ML,
  NNAPI, and GPU delegates).
keywords:
  - react-native
  - driver-license
  - identity-document
  - ocr
  - object-detection
  - nanodet
  - core-ml
  - tflite
  - on-device-ml
  - aamva
  - mrz
  - icao-9303
